From 47d5342275275010cda8bab0ffab033d441e6893 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 04:34:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] gomail-server: address add verifies admin-<gen>.cert and
 checks it with the log

Backlog item 63 (D93 addendum 23, AUDIT R48): "address add" read
admin-<gen>.cert once and trusted its identity_gen for the cascade check
without verifying the signature or comparing the certificate with the
log. It now reads it with store.ReadPlatformCertRaw, verifies the
signature with the key of identity_gen (pin identity list, above it the
valid logged successions, as client/read.go identityKey), runs the
cascade check on the authenticated identity_gen and then
Log.CheckPlatform on the same bytes. Failures are fail closed with the
new message adminCertInvalid. Client check rules are unchanged.

TestAddressAddForgedCert: admin-1.cert rewritten with identity_gen 2
under a pin that revokes identity 1 is refused before anything is
logged, both with a wrong signature and signed validly by identity 2
but not in the log. Counter-proof: with the signature check and
CheckPlatform disabled (and with CheckPlatform alone disabled) the test
fails; the refusal then comes only later from Append (admitAddress).

Prepared for after M1; to be merged after its own full run.

